spans.s:
वंश॑ m. cane, esp. of the bamboo;
 rafter, lath;
 reed-pipe,
flute (also f. ई);
 the spine;
 lineage, family, race.

वंशक m. a kind of sugar-cane;
 f. *वंशिका a kind of
flute, also = n. Agallochum.

वंशवर्धन a. increasing or propagating a race
(also ˚वर्धिन्);
 m. son.

वंश्य a. belonging to the main beam or to the family (—˚
= prec.);
 m. cross-beam, member of a family, ancestor or descendant.

वनग्रहण n. abstr. to seq. a.;
 ˚कोलाहल s.
hunting cry*

वनचर f. ई wandering in a forest;
 m. inhabitant of a
forest (man or animal).

{#{{vanajyosnI->vanajyotsnI||20160419|Jim Funderburk|https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/290|vana-jyotsnI ;
 missing 't' presumed misprint}}#} f. Light of the Grove (poet. N. of a
plant).*

वनमाला f. garland of wood flowers;
 poss. ˚लिन्, m. E.
of Kṛṣṇa.

वनर्गु॑ a. wandering in a forest or a wilderness;
 m. a
savage.

वनवासिन् a. living in a wood;
 m. forester, hermit,
ascetic.

व॑नस्प॑ति m. tree (lit. lord of the wood), esp. a
large tree with fruit, but without flowers;
 stem, trunk, beam, timber,
the sacrificial post;
 the Soma plant (as the lord of plants);
 E. of
Viṣṇu.

वनान्तर n. the interior of a forest;
 loc., acc., &
abl. in, into, & out of a forest.

वनाश्रय a. living in a forest;
 m. inhabitant of a
forest.

वनु॑स् a. eager, zealous;
 either devoted, loving, or
plotting, hostile. m. an enemy.

वनेचर f. ई wandering or dwelling in a forest;
 m.
inhabitant of a forest (either man or animal).

1 व॑न्दन m. N. of a man;
 n. praise, worship, reverential
greeting.

वन्ध्य a. barren, sterile (of women, female animals, &
plants);
 fruitless, useless, in vain;
 wanting, destitute of (—˚).
Abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

व॑न्य adj. living or growing in woods, sylvan, wild,
wooden;
 m. wild animal, (also n.) wild plant.

2 वानप्रस्थ a. relating to a hermit;
 m. the third
stage of a Brahman's life (also ˚प्रस्थ्य n.).

वानस्पत्य॑ a. relating to trees or woods, wooden;
 m.
tree, bush, plant i.g.;
 n. fruit of a tree.
